.nh
.TH "PB-PING" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-ping - Measure authenticated connectivity to a machine


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb ping <machine> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Measure authenticated connectivity to a machine

.PP
Send authenticated health exchanges to one enrolled device. --count and --timeout bound the measurements; a reachable transport alone is not a claim that the target service is ready.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--count\fP=4
	number of authenticated native connections

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for ping

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=10s
	timeout for each connection


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb(1)\fP
